sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant H as Handler
    participant F as Stream hub
    participant M as Notification multiplexer
    participant S as PageReader
    participant R as Redis
    C->>H: GET ?offset=now and live=sse
    H->>F: acquire provisional hub
    F->>M: register logical channel
    M->>R: SUBSCRIBE on one physical connection
    R-->>M: acknowledge current generation
    M-->>F: registration ready
    H->>S: ReadPage(path, offset) · capture first typed page
    S->>R: EVALSHA read.lua · metadata + optional bounded range
    S-->>H: first page · type · tail · closed · incarnation
    H->>F: initialize hub for that exact stream lifetime
    F-->>H: ready from authoritative page · no readiness reread
    H-->>C: 200 · Content-Type text/event-stream
    loop pages to the captured tail
        H-->>C: emit the page already held · data + control · flush
        H->>S: continuation ReadPage with same snapshot · no touch
    end
    H->>S: one no-touch stream identity confirmation
    H->>F: indexed attach at last flushed control offset
    R-->>M: append wake hint
    M-->>F: coalesced wake
    F->>S: one shared bounded ReadPage refresh
    F-->>H: shared immutable data event
    H-->>C: data then client control
    R-->>M: reconnect generation acknowledged
    M-->>F: coalesced reconnect event
    F->>S: immediate durable ReadPage NoTouch
    Note over H,R: no Store.Get and no :prod read (persistent and absolute-expiry-only refreshes are read-only)
    H-->>C: control streamClosed true → close
